[[13113,5085,"Failed to incorporate all the advice given by the tissue viability nurses in Mr [name redacted] care plans","incorporation of tissue viability advice",""],[13114,5085,"Failed to keep accurate records","inaccurate record keeping",""],[13115,5085,"Informed the CQC that the tissue viability nurses were still involved with Mr Farrington when they weren't","misrepresentation of nurse involvement",""],[13116,5085,"Failed to follow the advice of the tissue viability nurses as to turning and how to dress Mr [name redacted] sores","non-compliance with turning advice",""],[13117,5085,"Failed to refer Mr Farrington to his General Practitioner when he developed an infection in the sacral pressure sore on the 1st June 2016","failure to refer for infection",""],[13118,5085,"Only one tissue viability nurse was employed by First Community Care from March 2016 onwards. They were on annual leave for 6 weeks between the 18th 2 March and the 15th June 2016. This was not an adequate level service","inadequate nurse staffing",""]]